{"name":"Hydrargyrum","hex":"#9b9b9b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hydrargyrum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mercury (chemical element)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hydrargyrum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mercury (element)","blocks":[{"text":"Mercury is a chemical element; it has symbol Hg and atomic number 80. It is commonly known as quicksilver. A heavy, silvery d-block element, mercury is the only metallic element that is known to be liquid at standard temperature and pressure. As well as having the lowest freezing point, mercury has the lowest boiling point and subsequently the narrowest liquid state range of any metal at standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Pouring_liquid_mercury_bionerd.jpg/330px-Pouring_liquid_mercury_bionerd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(element)","wikidata":"Q925"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/500px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/1280px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg/500px-Pound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A round pound coin (density ~7.6 g/cm3) floats on mercury due to the buoyancy force upon it and appears to float higher because of the strong surface tension of the mercury.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APound-coin-floating-in-mercury.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Mercury-27128.jpg/500px-Mercury-27128.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Mercury-27128.jpg/500px-Mercury-27128.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Native mercury with cinnabar, Socrates mine, Sonoma County, California. Cinnabar sometimes alters to native mercury in the oxidized zone of mercury deposits.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMercury-27128.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/HgProductionPrice.png/500px-HgProductionPrice.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/HgProductionPrice.png/1280px-HgProductionPrice.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/HgProductionPrice.png/500px-HgProductionPrice.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Evolution of mercury price (U.S.) and production (worldwide)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHgProductionPrice.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Amalgam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Amalgam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Dental amalgam filling a decayed molar tooth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmalgam.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/2023_Rt%C4%99ciowy_termometr_lekarski.jpg/250px-2023_Rt%C4%99ciowy_termometr_lekarski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/2023_Rt%C4%99ciowy_termometr_lekarski.jpg/500px-2023_Rt%C4%99ciowy_termometr_lekar